 "die_obligations": [
  "drop 16 regional clocks per cluster instance (dv2r8f: 48 instances -> 768 regional clock drops) at the cluster's 16 regional clock pins (face pins of the contract: rows 0 / 3 on the S / N face, rows 1 / 2 on the W / E face, M4; the die may also feed them as centre area pins); each region builds its own local tree",
  "NO phase alignment owed for data (Q-CLUSTER-LANDALL replaces Q-CL16-EARLY's +/-60 ps): every multi-bit region crossing is landed (D 4, E = K = 2), so it tolerates any region-to-region skew dL in the window (2 - 4) T + t_hold < dL < 2 T - t_cq - t_setup (T = 833.3: about -1666 .. +1666 ps) at TT and FF.  The die keeps the drops of COMMUNICATING region pairs within +/-400 ps of each other (TT and FF) only for the cluster SDC's inter-region uncertainty; Q-CB16RST: no 1-bit reset hop crosses a region seam any more (regional resets below), so no in-cluster single-cycle path depends on region-to-region skew",
  "boundary ports are timed against the region that holds their pin register (port_domains); the die's neighbour links into / out of the cluster land against THAT region's clock (LANDING-CONTRACT)",
  "REGIONAL RESETS (Q-CB16RST 10-19, replaces the single rst_n): 16 reset pins rst_c<c>r<r> per instance (beside each ck_c<c>r<r>; 48 instances -> 768 drops).  The die releases all 16 of an instance on the SAME die calendar edge, each delivered on (and timed against) its own region clock: the die reset tree LANDS each drop (fixed latency, calendared release).  Each pin is registered at its region entry (u_fab.u_rpin_<q>, ROOT-RST); in-cluster depth unchanged: tiles / xstn 19 edges after the pin, landing epochs at each landing's common depth (G == R0, warm-up 25 edges).  A slip of one region by one edge breaks the landings (bench MUT 8 FAILs).",
  "the cluster's port latencies grow (compiler record below): the die schedule takes tap / bco / rs / rs_i->rs_o from compiler.latency_edges"
 ],
